negative/E0306_scoped_thread_closure_not_send.cryo a closure written without `move` given to the scope's `spawn` is refused only when what it uses is not thread-safe (the scope's handle, an `Rc`), where the baseline refused the borrowing control too
fix_shows_type_arguments each E0307 asking for type arguments shows the call with them written in, and a literal owner's call names the owner's own type parameters, where the baseline filled in the argument it inferred, which may not be the one meant
fix_shows_borrow_or_clone a move out of storage that still owns the value shows the `.clone()` as an edited line and the `&` of a field or element as help only, where the baseline offered the `&` as an edit that need not compile
fix_shows_removed_form_replacement `public module` and `implement class` show their replacement as an edit, and a constructor and destructor show the Cryo shape as an example, where the baseline printed the help alone
fix_shows_address_and_constant_path a struct cast to a pointer shows the cast of its address, and a type's constant read through a value names the path through the type as help, where the baseline offered the path as an uncertain edit
fix_shows_missing_bound a method, a static, an object conversion and a `?` conversion the bounds do not allow show the signature with the bound added, where the baseline printed the help alone
fix_shows_recursive_type_example a recursive struct shows its field behind a pointer as an example, where the baseline printed the help alone
fix_shows_escape_digit `\8` shows the literal with the digit written without its backslash, where the baseline printed the help alone
drop_call_on_type_parameter_help the missing-bound help on a type parameter's method shows the signature with the bound added, where the baseline printed the help alone
moved_value_clone_hint a type without Clone shows `with [Clone]` on its declaration as an example, where the baseline printed the help alone
call_through_dereferenced_unbounded_pointer_fix `(*p)()` for a type parameter with no callable bound shows the bound with placeholders for the parts the call cannot decide, where the baseline guessed them from the call
callable_bound_without_return_fix a callable bound missing its return type gets help only, where the baseline offered `-> void` as an edit the callable may not fit
closure_move_fixes a moved capture and a `move` closure that takes a value still used get help only, where the baseline offered `move` and its removal as edits that need not compile
fix_shows_clone_of_dereference the clone fix for a moved dereference writes `(*r).clone()`, where the baseline offered `*r.clone()` as a certain edit, which clones the reference
numeric_conversion_fix a numeric conversion that may change the value gets the `as` as help only, where the baseline offered it as an edit
operator_bound_fix an operator's missing bound shows placeholders for the operand and output types it cannot know, where the baseline guessed them
quick_fixes removing a `?` whose operand already has the expected type is a certain edit, where the baseline marked it uncertain
thread_builder_borrowing_closure_fix a borrowing closure given to a thread builder gets help to write `move`, where the baseline offered it as an edit that need not compile
thread_spawn_borrowing_closure_fix a borrowing closure given to `thread::spawn` gets help to write `move`, where the baseline offered it as an edit that need not compile
fix_shows_method_call a method read as a field that takes nothing but its read-only receiver shows the call as an edit, where the baseline printed the help alone
struct_measured_through_pointer_cycle a struct reaching, through a pointer field, a struct that holds it by value is copied whole, where the baseline measured it before its body was set and a returned literal lost a field
negative/E0229_mixed_operands_neither_holds_the_other.cryo numeric operands with no type holding both are E0229, where the baseline computed `i32 + u32` as `u32` and `i64 * f64` as `f64` with a warning
negative/E0200_compound_assignment_computes_wider.cryo a compound assignment whose computed type the target cannot hold is E0200, where the baseline stored the wider result truncated
negative/E0200_pointer_sized_integer_conversions.cryo a conversion into or out of `usize`/`isize` that loses values on some target is E0200, where the baseline took `usize` as `u64` and `isize` as `i64`
negative/E0214_argument_would_change_value.cryo an argument whose parameter cannot hold every value of it is E0214, where the baseline passed `i64` to `f64`, `u64` to `i64` and `i8` to `u64`
negative/E0229_numeric_plus_string.cryo a refused binary operation computes no value, so its initializer reports nothing more, where the baseline added an E0200 for the left operand's type
lambda_in_stdlib_generic_instance a lambda in a stdlib generic method is internal to the module emitting it, where the baseline stripped the program's definition as one the archive provides and `Array<i64>.sort` compared through another instance's lambda
match_arm_widens_by_its_own_sign a match arm narrower than the match widens by its own signedness, where the baseline sign-extended a `u32` arm into an `i64` match
borrow_written_with_mut_fix `&mut x` is E0101 at the `mut` with one fix deleting it, where the baseline reported E0100 twice with insertions that did not compile
expected_token_offers_no_insertion an "expected `;`" or "expected `=>`" error offers no insertion, where the baseline offered `{ big; }` and `_ =>=> {`
numeric_refusal_help_converts_with_as E0229 and a compound assignment's E0200 give "convert with `as`" as a help line, where the baseline wrote it into the message
negative/E0010_pointer_sized_literal_past_32_bits.cryo a `usize` or `isize` literal past what 32 bits hold is E0010, where the baseline took a 64-bit value
stdlib/array_sort.cryo `Array.sort` hands `sort_by` a lambda, which is internal to the module emitting it, where the baseline linked the program's `Array<i64>` instance to another instance's lambda and sorted by the low 16 bits; the file's own lambdas are internal now, so its object moves
negative/E0251_read_only_container_for_a_method_writable_slice.cryo a read-only `&Array<T>` for a method's `mut &Slice<T>` is E0251 and the writable control call binds, where the baseline also refused the control as a method that does not exist (E0358)
field_read_releases_temporary a `Copy` field read off a call's result or a struct literal, through any number of fields, releases the value when the statement ends, where the baseline copied the field out and never released the value (exit 2: no release ran)
type_declaration_without_type_fix `trait Bump` written without `type` is refused at `trait` with a machine-applicable insertion of `type `, where the baseline refused `Bump` as a missing `;` and offered `->` replaced with `.` inside the trait
iterator_collect_sum_rev_peek_flat_map `collect` and `sum` call `C::from_iterator(this)` and `S::sum(this)`, where the baseline left both calls unbound in every copy of the tests (E0900) though the project's own main builds
type_declaration_without_type_help `struct Pair` written without `type`, with an error of its own in the body, is refused with help text, and `point->x` with no fix, where the baseline offered `->` replaced with `.` as machine-applicable
